// ztest: native pytest-style multi-process test orchestrator for Project Zahlen.
//
// Consumes first-party Zahlen extensions (<CommandLine/CommandLine.hpp>,
// <Signal/SignalManager.hpp>) and Core headers (<Zahlen/Core/Print.hpp>,
// <Zahlen/Core/Defer.hpp>) without linking `zahlen_engine`, reads
// <build_dir>/ztest_manifest.txt generated by
// cmake/ZTest.cmake, discovers reflected C++26 `namespace ZHLN::Test` `test_*`
// functions and primary-TU suites via worker `--ztest-list` with live cold-start
// feedback, shards CPU execution per source file (`--file`) across `-j N`
// isolated worker processes while pooling GPU workers per binary, streams
// structured `@@ZTEST` events, enforces per-worker wall-clock watchdogs, and
// respawns workers with `--skip-until` if an individual case crashes or hangs.

